    "b-10-document-node-vocabulary-stays-sm-11": {
      "id": "b-10-document-node-vocabulary-stays-sm-11",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Node vocabulary stays small and closed"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-document-decision-new-node-t-12": {
      "id": "b-10-document-decision-new-node-t-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision.",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " New node types are added only when the existing block vocabulary\ncannot represent a common prompt structure. Prompt-structure conventions map\nonto the existing vocabulary rather than getting their own node types: a\nworkflow is a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "section",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " tagged "
        },
        {
          "insert": "workflow",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " with nested phase sections, steps\nare "
        },
        {
          "insert": "orderedList",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " nodes, constraints are lists, and single-output skeletons\nuse "
        },
        {
          "insert": "codeBlock",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " inside an output-format section. No workflow-specific or\ntechnique-specific node types exist."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-document-why-a-small-closed-13": {
      "id": "b-10-document-why-a-small-closed-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why.",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " A small closed vocabulary keeps renderers, transforms, and validation\ntotal over one canonical AST, every consumer handles every node."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-10-document-applies-to-a-new-pr-14": {
      "id": "b-10-document-applies-to-a-new-pr-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Applies to.",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " A new prompt convention is expressed with existing nodes\nfirst; a vocabulary extension needs a structure the current nodes cannot\nrepresent."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
